<title>CANADA: Estimates - Saskatchewan crop quality.</title>
<headline>Estimates - Saskatchewan crop quality.</headline>
<dateline>WINNIPEG 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saskatchewan's grain, oilseed and specialty crop quality was estimated by Saskatchewan Wheat Pool in its final crop report of the year on data up to Nov 4.</p>
<p>	   CROP QUALITY TO NOV 4</p>
<p>CROP     No1	No2     No3	No4</p>
<p>	  '96 5-yr '96 5-yr '96 5-yr '96 5-yr</p>
<p>S.Wheat  42  47   20  25   29  16    9  12</p>
<p>Durum    25  30   21  33   25  28   29   9</p>
<p>Oats	3   7   26  21   59  68   12   4</p>
<p>Barley   23  26   58  65   15   8    4   2</p>
<p>Flax     98  96    2   4</p>
<p>Canola   82  82   15  13    3   4    0   1</p>
<p>Peas     19   4   39  23   27  11   15  62</p>
<p>Lentils  47  26   30  18   21  33    2  23</p>
<p>Mustard  78  83   13   7    7   7    2   3</p>
<p>W.Wheat  49  --   25  --    8  --   18  --</p>
<p>Rye	70  67   26  22    3   8    1   3</p>
<p>--Gilbert Le Gras 204-947-3548</p>
</text>
